# UI naming — no abbreviations

Never use abbreviations when referring to view components or UI in code, comments, docs, or conversation about iOS or Android apps.

## Floating action controls

- Say and write **FloatingActionButton**, never **FAB**, **Fab**, or **fab** (wrap or alias Material 3's `FloatingActionButton` using the full name).
- Stacks of those controls use **FloatingActionColumn** / **floatingActionColumn**.
- Property and symbol names must spell this out (`applyFloatingActionButton`, `floatingActionColumn`), not shortened forms.

## General

- Prefer full, readable type and property names for reusable UI (`SharedListCell`, `FloatingActionItem`, etc.) across both SwiftUI Views and Jetpack Compose `@Composable` functions.
- Do not introduce acronym-style UI nicknames in new code or when renaming existing symbols.
